# Files git should never track, anywhere in this project.
#
# This is the only ignore file. There used to be one of these in backend/ and
# another in frontend/, both saying the same things as this one, which meant
# three places to check when something was committed that should not have been.
#
# Two rules worth knowing:
#   1. Installed packages are never committed. Anyone can rebuild them from
#      package-lock.json with "npm install", and committing them adds tens of
#      thousands of files nobody wrote.
#   2. Secrets and real data are never committed. .env holds API keys, and the
#      SQLite file holds real people's details.

# Installed packages
node_modules/

# Build output
dist/
dist-ssr/
build/

# Secrets. .env.example IS committed, because it is only a blank template.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Vite's convention: anything ending .local is yours and is never committed.
*.local

# The SQLite database and its temporary write-ahead files.
# It is rebuilt automatically the first time the server starts.
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Editor and operating system clutter
.DS_Store
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
*.swp

# Test coverage output
coverage/

# Vite cache
.vite/
